#> source: =
# 5. Number lines. Pement: sed = filename | sed 'N;s/\n/\t/'
# = prints the current line number on its own line, before the line itself.
# The sheet pipes that through a second sed that joins each pair with a tab;
# here only the first half runs, so the numbers appear above the lines.
# Count lines instead with  sed -n '$='  (the number of the last line only).
# Try: #ARGS -n  on the line above  $=  and watch the output shrink to "5".
=

